   "text": "I read the drawing as a macrocycle built from two ornithines, an N\u2011methyl tryptophan and a diaryl sulfide linker, and wrote the SMILES from that.\n\n**Linker.** A pyridine carries the CH2\u2013NH at C3 and the sulfur at C2. The sulfur joins to a benzene ring. On that benzene, the carbon next to the C\u2013S carbon bears CH2\u2013NH. Going round the ring, the next carbon bears the 4\u2011carboxyphenyl group, then two CH carbons, then a Cl\u2011bearing carbon that sits next to the C\u2013S carbon.\n\n**Peptide chain.** Going round the ring from the pyridine side:\n1. The first ornithine has an NH\u2013CH2 link to the pyridine, a CH2CH2CH2NH2 side chain on a wedge, and a C(=O) that leads to the next residue's NH.\n2. The second ornithine has an NH, a wedged CH2CH2CH2NH2 side chain, and a C(=O) bonded to the N\u2011methyl nitrogen.\n3. The N\u2011methyl tryptophan has a wedged CH2\u2011indol\u20113\u2011yl side chain and a C(=O) bonded to the NH\u2013CH2 on the benzene ring.\n\n**Stereochemistry.** Each of the three \u03b1\u2011carbons has a wedged side chain and an implicit hydrogen pointing away. Priorities N > C(=O) > CH2 > H run counterclockwise on the page in each case, so all three are S (L\u2011amino acids). I converted this to @/@@ by neighbour order in the SMILES string.\n\nSMILES: NCCC[C@@H]1NCc2cccnc2Sc2c(Cl)ccc(-c3ccc(C(=O)O)cc3)c2CNC(=O)[C@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](CCCN)NC1=O"
